ld check the returning values of every function.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery0\footery994\margtsxn1060\margbsxn1200\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri623\sl240\slmult1\sb76\f0\fs24\b0 The main factor in determining whether the image is live or spoofed is the liveness value (probability). An image can be considered live if the liveness value is higher than 0.5. An additional factor to consider is the image_quality value, which measures how "appropriate" the image is for the liveness check. Images with quality values lower than 0.5 should generally be rejected. Both measurements are float values in the range of [0, 1].\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb5\f0\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri903\qj\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs24\b0 Sometimes an image may be rejected. If this happens, you can get a liveness check error message in the attributes variable after the "LivenessError=" prefix. An example of\expnd-5\expndtw-25  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 error parsing in\expnd0\expndtw-1  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 C++:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\f9\fs24\b0 string e = "LivenessError=";\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li801\fi-581\ri2332\sl240\slmult1\sb4\f9\fs24\b0 if (string(attributes).find(e) != string::npos) \'7B string livenessErrorMessage =\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl-268\f9\fs24\b0 string(attributes).substr(e.length());\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\sb3\f9\fs24\b0\charscalex100 \'7D\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f9\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs24\b0 When using the Tracker API with the iBeta add-on, you should set the following parameters:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri772\qj\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f9\fs24\b0 FSDK_SetTrackerParameter(tracker, "DetectLiveness",\expnd-9\expndtw-47  \f9\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 "true"); FSDK_SetTrackerParameter(tracker,\expnd-8\expndtw-41  \f9\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 "SmoothAttributeLiveness", "false");\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri697\sl240\slmult1\f9\fs24\b0 FSDK_SetTrackerParameter(tracker, "AttributeLivenessSmoothingAlpha", "1"); FSDK_SetTrackerParameter(tracker, "LivenessFramesCount", "1");\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb6\f9\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\qj\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs24\b0 Sample code in C++ for Tracker API:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb8\f0\fs23\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl-271\sb1\f9\fs24\b0 HImage image;\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri6221\sl242\slmult1\f9\fs24\b0 char attributes[1024]; char err[1024];\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri5514\sl242\slmult1\f9\fs24\b0 float liveness = 0.0f; float image_quality =\expnd-3\expndtw-16  \f9\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 0.0f;\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl-268\f9\fs24\b0 std::string e = "LivenessError=";\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb7\f9\fs23\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl-271\sb1\f9\fs24\b0 while (!is_finished) \'7B\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\fi580\sl240\slmult1\f9\fs24\b0 FSDK_FeedFrame(tracker, camera, image, &count, ids, 256 * sizeof(long long));\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\fi580\sl240\slmult1\f9\fs24\b0 FSDK_GetTrackerFacialAttribute(tracker, camera, ids[0], "Liveness", attributes, 1024);\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\fi580\ri600\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f9\fs24\b0 FSDK_GetValueConfidence(attributes, "Liveness", &liveness);\par