{\pard\plain\intbl\s7\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li100\ri117\sl240\slmult1\sb99\f0\fs22\b0 FaceSDK/data FaceSDK/FaceSdk.fra mework FaceSDK/libfsdk- static.a FaceSDK/LuxandFace SDK.h\cell}\row\pard\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs26\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs29\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s3\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\sb1{\*\bkmkstart Image requirements}{\*\bkmkend Image requirements}{\*\bkmkstart _bookmark148}{\*\bkmkend _bookmark148}\f7\fs32\b1 Image requirements\par\pard\plain\s4\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\sb237{\*\bkmkstart Image format}{\*\bkmkend Image format}{\*\bkmkstart _bookmark149}{\*\bkmkend _bookmark149}\f13\fs26\b1 Image format\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri417\sl240\slmult1\sb63\f0\fs24\b0 Lossless formats are preferred, as lossy compression can negatively affect accuracy. If you use lossy formats, make sure the compression is at a minimal level. For example, for JPEG, 70 is the lowest practical compression level.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb5\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s4\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1{\*\bkmkstart Image resolution}{\*\bkmkend Image resolution}{\*\bkmkstart _bookmark150}{\*\bkmkend _bookmark150}\f13\fs26\b1 Image resolution\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\sb63\f0\fs24\b0 The iBeta Liveness add-on processes the area around the face, so the optimal resolution will depend on the image composition. Assuming a portrait orientation with the face centered and occupying at least 1/4 of the image area, the recommended image resolution range is from{\*\bkmkstart Image composition}{\*\bkmkend Image composition}{\*\bkmkstart _bookmark151}{\*\bkmkend _bookmark151} 600x800 to 960x1280.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb9\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s4\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\f13\fs26\b1 Image composition\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f13\fs24\b1\i0\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-360\ri376\sl242\slmult1\sb1\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 There should be only one main face in the image. It should be fully visible within the frame, fully open, and without any occlusions. Cropping is not allowed. Small faces\expnd-4\expndtw-19  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 in the background are not taken into\expnd0\expndtw1  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 account.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-270\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The minimum size of a face box that can be processed is 150x150\expnd-3\expndtw-16  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 pixels.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-275\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The padding between the face box and the image's borders should be at least 15\expnd-4\expndtw-21  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 pixels.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-275\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The distance between the pupils on the face should be at least 50\expnd-4\expndtw-19  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 pixels.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery0\footery994\margtsxn1060\margbsxn1200\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-360\ri915\sl240\slmult1\sb76\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The out-of-plane rotation angle (face pitch and yaw) should be no more than\expnd-4\expndtw-22  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 \'B130 degrees.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri1133\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs24\b0 Images that do not meet these conditions will be rejected. Other factors that can affect accuracy include:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb8\f0\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-360\ri400\sl240\slmult1\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Motion blur can significantly increase BPCER (the rate of errors classifying a\expnd-5\expndtw-27  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 genuine person as a\expnd0\expndtw-2  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 spoof).\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-360\ri1151\sl240\slmult1\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Texture filtering can significantly increase APCER (the rate of errors\expnd-6\expndtw-30  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 allowing impostors through).\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-274\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Spotlights on the face and nearby surroundings can significantly increase\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 BPCER.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-275\sb2\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Poorly lit environments and colored lighting can significantly increase\expnd-2\expndtw-11  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 BPCER.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-275\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Fish-eye lenses are not\expnd0\expndtw-1  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 supported.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-275\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Sunglasses may cause\expnd0\expndtw-2  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 confusion.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s4\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\sb1{\*\bkmkstart Sample images}{\*\bkmkend Sample images}{\*\bkmkstart _bookmark152}{\*\bkmkend _bookmark152}\f13\fs26\b1 Sample images\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f13\fs24\b1\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs24\b0 This section contains image samples categorized into three groups:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-275\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Good samples: Images with optimal face size, positioning, and lighting\expnd-3\expndtw-16  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 conditions.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-360\ri543\sl242\slmult1\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Acceptable but suboptimal samples: Images that are acceptable but were taken\expnd-6\expndtw-30  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 under less-than-ideal\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 conditions.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-274\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Incorrect samples: Images that are not acceptable for\expnd-2\expndtw-9  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 processing.\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s4\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1{\*\bkmkstart Good examples}{\*\bkmkend Good examples}{\*\bkmkstart _bookmark153}{\*\bkmkend _bookmark153}\f13\fs26\b1 Good examples\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb7\f13\fs13\b1\i0\par
