\par}}}}\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\sb76\f0\fs24\b0 The face is positioned incorrectly, partially out of frame:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs38\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s3\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1{\*\bkmkstart Configuration files}{\*\bkmkend Configuration files}{\*\bkmkstart _bookmark156}{\*\bkmkend _bookmark156}\f7\fs32\b1 Configuration files\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri388\sl242\slmult1\sb120\f0\fs24\b0 It is possible to change internal parameters used to validate the image. Lower values will result in fewer images being rejected, but accuracy may degrade for such images. The parameters are defined in the \f1\fs24\b1\i0 data/preprocessing/face_params.conf \f0\fs24\b0\i0 file.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl-270\f0\fs24\b0 Available parameters:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-275\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 min_face_size: Minimum width and height of the face box, in pixels (150 -\expnd-2\expndtw-11  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 default).\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-360\ri447\sl240\slmult1\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 min_face_size_relative: Minimum relative width and height of the face box, as a\expnd-6\expndtw-28  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 ratio of the face's width and height to the image's width and height. Defined as a value between 0 and 1. For example, if the value is 0.25, one side of the face box should be at least a quarter of the image's corresponding side (0.15 -\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 default).\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-360\ri597\sl240\slmult1\sb1\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 detectable_face_size_relative: Similar to the parameter above, but if the size of the face box is smaller than this value, the face is simply skipped. This is used as a\expnd-7\expndtw-33  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 filter for small faces in the background (0.075 -\expnd0\expndtw-2  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 default).\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-360\ri578\sl242\slmult1\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 min_pupillary_distance: Minimum distance between the pupils on the face, in\expnd-5\expndtw-26  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 pixels (50 -\expnd0\expndtw-2  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 default).\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-360\ri836\sl240\slmult1\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 min_face_padding: Minimum distance from the image's border to the face box,\expnd-5\expndtw-25  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 in pixels (15 -\expnd0\expndtw1  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 default).\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-274\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 max_roll: Maximum roll angle of the head, in degrees (45 -\expnd0\expndtw2  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 default).\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl-276\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 max_yaw: Maximum yaw angle of the head, in degrees (30 -\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 default).\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s6\ls7\ilvl1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li941\fi-361\sl240\slmult1\tx940\tx941\f0\fs24\b0\i0 max_pitch: Maximum pitch angle of the head, in degrees (30 -\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 default).\f10\fs20\cf1\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb5\f0\fs31\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s2\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1{\*\bkmkstart Working with Cameras}{\*\bkmkend Working with Cameras}{\*\bkmkstart _bookmark157}{\*\bkmkend _bookmark157}\f7\fs40\b1 Working with Cameras\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri333\qj\sl240\slmult1\sb54\f0\fs24\b0 The library offers a set of functions to work with DirectShow/v4l2-compatible web cameras and IP cameras with an MJPEG interface. The functions allow single frames to be retrieved from\expnd-3\expndtw-15  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd-3\expndtw-15  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 camera\expnd-3\expndtw-14  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 one-by-one;\expnd-3\expndtw-15  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 they\expnd-3\expndtw-13  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 are\expnd-3\expndtw-15  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 stored\expnd-3\expndtw-13  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 in\expnd-3\expndtw-14  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 HImage\expnd-3\expndtw-14  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 descriptors.\expnd-3\expndtw-14  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 The\expnd-3\expndtw-15  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 application\expnd-3\expndtw-13  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 usually\expnd-3\expndtw-14  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 grabs frames in a loop, displaying each frame in its window and performing manipulations with images (such as face\expnd0\expndtw-1  \f0\fs24\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 detection).\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri334\qj\sl244\slmult1\sb121\f0\fs24\b0 Web camera functions are available only for Windows and Linux platforms. IP camera functions are available for all platforms.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery0\footery994\margtsxn1060\margbsxn1200\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1\sb76\f0\fs24\b0 Android and iOS samples include platform-specific code working with cameras on phones and tablets.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs31\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s3\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\sl240\slmult1{\*\bkmkstart Data Types}{\*\bkmkend Data Types}{\*\bkmkstart _bookmark158}{\*\bkmkend _bookmark158}\f7\fs32\b1 Data Types\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li220\ri266\sl242\slmult1\sb121\f0\fs24\b0 There are data types to store the information about video